<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 56,578 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 56,578 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 56,578 tonnes of export and import cargo in 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Thursday compared to 46,335 tonnes in the same period on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Thursday    Jan 1</p>
<p>    Export cargo		16,169	15,269</p>
<p>    Import cargo		40,409	31,066</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, three ships sailed and five berthed. In the next 24 hours, eight are expected to sail and 11 are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Palm oil		 18,000	 Wawasan Courage    2/01</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 25,000	 Miraj		  3/01</p>
<p>High speed diesel    56,000	 Keefan		 3/01</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     31,500	 Capitan Elias	3/01</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     31,769	 Zhad Shan	    5/01</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
